{
	"_about": "alder: a 20s horizon-montage launch film, derived frame-by-frame from a 20.0s model-launch film (1920x1080 @25fps). Authored on the 1280x720 stage (stage px = reference px / 1.5) and rendered at device scale 1.5: render.mjs --fps 25 --scale 1.5. Placeholder product: Lumen 2, by Alder. Every shot is the curved edge of something laid across the middle of the frame as a horizon; hard cuts land on that edge, accelerating, while a three-beat serif line stands on it and steps larger at every cut. A planet-limb horizon opens the film and the end card pans up onto it, so the film loops.",
	"_sections": "S1 planet-limb horizon, haze breathing outward 0-1.24 | S2 36 horizon plates (image slots with generated stand-in textures), cuts accelerating 1.04s -> 0.20s, 1.24-15.96 | S3 the line on the horizon, 'Look' over 5 plates 8.72-10.68, 'a little' over 5 10.68-12.48, 'closer' over 13 12.48-15.96, re-set larger at every cut and bent to the later plates | S4 name card 15.96-17.28, wordmark 17.28-20.00, the whole card pans up 545 px 18.20-20.00 and lands on the opening frame",
	"_slots": "36 image slots, 'plate-01'..'plate-36' (s2-plate-NN: set 'src' to a photo; it is clipped to the body below the edge, top-aligned at the edge, so frame the photo with its subject's curved edge near the top). Each slot's 'label' says what the reference showed there. Without 'src' the plate's 'layers' generate a stand-in texture in the reference's colours.",
